      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I got mine fixed (after trying EVERY other fix, including looking for nonexistent Google certs, youtube-dl.exe update, reinstalls, cache clears, the works). Actual fix was from ghostdude00 a bit down on this thread. Just installing both x64 ***and x86*** (64-bit and 32-bit) versions of Visual Studio C++ from here did the trick: https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/2977003/the-latest-supported-visual-c-downloads\n\nx86: vc_redist.x86.exe\n\nx64: vc_redist.x64.exe\n\nThen restart VRChat (or better yet your whole machine), and try loading a YouTube URL in any of the easily searchable 'theater' Worlds to test.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
