      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "same issue for me.\nManaged to fix it through the following attempts:\n- installed latest VC Redist x64 and x86 from https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/2977003/the-latest-supported-visual-c-downloads\n- restarted computer when asked by the installer\n- tested the video player in my homeworld without success\n- downloaded the latest youtube-dl.exe from https://ytdl-org.github.io/youtube-dl/download.html and replaced the one in the VRChat installationfolder (VRChat_Data\\StreamingAssets)\n- restarted the game and the player in my homeworld works now.\nSo if someone else who has this issue can please confirm if just updating your youtube-dl.exe is enough or if more steps are needed, this might allow the VRChat devs to push out a fix for this.\nEdit: playing through Steam on a Windows 10 system",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
